hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1835","Ismail ibn Umar Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ali al-Zarrad who said: Jafar ibn Tamam ibn Abbas narrated to me, from his father who said: They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he was brought, and he said: Why do I see you coming to me with yellow teeth? Use the tooth-stick. Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my nation, I would have made the tooth-stick obligatory upon them as I made ablution obligatory upon them."
"1836","Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to line up Abd Allah and Ubayd Allah and Kathir from the sons of Abbas, then say: Whoever races to me first shall have such-and-such. He said: So they would race to him and fall upon his back and chest, and he would kiss them and embrace them."
